      "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y = f\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}x\\right),$ we take the graph of $y = f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $2$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $2.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218944/assets/ae191c7f3af5c16113d28c20572eba4559b08145327cab651a49ca7d39991502.png)",
